// P3C.2 / D1.7, D2.7, D2.9, D4.1–D4.11, D7.1–D7.5, D8.4, D8.5, X6, X7: views of a part, following
// ex1-step4..ex1-step6 and the lesson images, on the bracket stand-in (`samples::drawing_bracket`: a plate
// with four Ø10 holes and R10 corners, an upright with a Ø24 hole, an R15 corner and a 20 mm
// chamfer), on an ANSI_A_INCH sheet (third angle). Sheet mm → screen px: x = 271 + 3.915·x,
// y = 943 − 3.915·y.
// 01 The bracket in Part Studio 1 (its part is "Bracket").
// 02 D1.7: "+" → Create Drawing… → ANSI_A_INCH → OK opens the drawing with Insert view already
//    running: the Insert view card (reference, orientation, scale, "None") and the Select a part
//    or assembly browser (Current document, Main, Part Studios, search, filters, the studio
//    expanded to its part) (ex1-step4.png).
// 03 D4.2, D4.3, D8.4: the part Bracket picked, Front, 1:2: the view follows the cursor in blue.
// 04 D4.4: placed; the tool is now Projected view and the title block reads "Bracket" and 1:2.
//    Moving up previews the Top view above (third angle).
// 05 Top placed; moving right previews Right. 06 Right placed; moving up-right previews the
//    Isometric view.
// 07 Isometric placed, Esc ends the tool (ex1-step5.png layout).
// 08 D4.8: the isometric view's context menu (lesson-view-context-menu.png).
// 09 D2.9, D4.7: View properties: the reference (with its link), Scale 1:4 picked, the sheet.
// 10 D4.9: OK, then Show shaded view: the isometric view at 1:4, shaded in the part's colour.
// 11 D4.11: Front's Tangent edges submenu (Hidden, Solid ✓, Phantom).
// 12 D4.10, D4.11, D8.5: hidden lines shown and tangent edges Phantom on Front, Top and Right:
//    the plate's holes dashed in Front and Right, the upright's hole dashed in Top, the rounded
//    corners' tangent edges in long-short-short phantom (ex1-step6.png).
// 13 D7.1, D7.2: Front dragged left and down: Top follows it sideways, Right down, both still
//    aligned.
// 14 D7.1: Right → Suppress alignment with parent, then dragged up and right: it moves freely.
// 15 D7.4: Show/hide sketches… on Front: the studio's sketches as a searchable checklist, Sketch 2
//    ticked; 16 its curves drawn (blue) over the view.
// 17 D2.7: Ctrl+S: Sheet1 → Bracket → Front → Top, Right, Isometric.
// 18 D4.6: on a new Sheet2, a Front view; Auxiliary view, its chamfer edge highlighted under the
//    cursor; 19 the view folded out from it follows the cursor along the fold line; 20 placed: the
//    chamfer face at its true size.
// 21 D7.3: a Sheet3 inserted; Front (on Sheet2) → Move to sheet… → Sheet3.
// 22 Sheet2 keeps the auxiliary view (children don't move); 23 Front is on Sheet3.
// 24 D7.5: Align view vertical, the chamfer edge highlighted; 25 the view turned so the chamfer
//    edge is vertical.
Scenario(
    start: Some("document"),
    steps: [
        WaitFor("document-shell"),
        Wait(30),
        Custom("drawing-bracket"),
        Wait(60),
